  "instructions": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "kind": "prep",
      "primary_message": "Cut the boneless pork shoulder into 2-inch cubes. Finely chop the onion. Grate the garlic on microplane grater. Finely chop the roasted poblano and keep it frozen until you use it. Finely crumble the queso fresco.",
      "secondary_message": "0.68 kg boneless pork shoulder\n1 small onion\n2 medium cloves garlic\n1 roasted poblano, fresh, or canned\n1 cup queso fresco, cotija, or feta"
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "primary_message": "Heat vegetable oil in a large Dutch oven over high heat until smoking. Add pork shoulder and brown on all sides, about 10 minutes total. Transfer to a large plate.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "primary_message": "Reduce heat to medium-high. Add onions and garlic and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened but not browned, about 4 minutes. Add chile and chicken stock and scrape up browned bits with a wooden spoon. Return pork to the pot along with bay leaves. Bring to a boil, then reduce to a bare simmer. Cover and cook until pork is completely tender, about 2 1/2 hours.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "primary_message": "Remove pork from pot with a slotted spoon and transfer to a medium bowl. Discard bay leaves, and increase heat to high. Boil until liquid is reduced to 1/2 cup. Meanwhile, shred pork with 2 forks. Add liquid to pork and season to taste with salt and pepper (it may not need any salt).",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "primary_message": "Set aside while you make the Venezuelan-style arepas. Split arepas, stuff with pork, top with crumbled cheese and cilantro, and serve with lime wedges and avocado slices if desired.",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
